{
  "id": "COMPOUND:36265 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "Tiegusanin L appears to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a chain of targets, with LoVo cells acting as a central mediator. The evidence suggests that Tiegusanin L targets LoVo, which in turn is targeted by both (+)-(6S)-hydroxymenthol and Discorhabdine A, all of which ultimately engage the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This implies that Tiegusanin L may influence the activity of these compounds, potentially through a shared mechanism involving LoVo cells. The presence of multiple pathways converging on the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex suggests a possible role in the regulation of gene expression, possibly through epigenetic modifications. The integration of these findings highlights the importance of LoVo as a potential intermediate in the interaction network, reinforcing the notion that Tiegusanin L may modulate the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex in a context-dependent manner.",
